&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="cherry-hallway-console"&gt;Cherry Hallway Console (Proposed)&lt;/a&gt; — narrow entry console, mortise-and-tenon cherry, drawbored — designed, not yet built&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</description></item><item><title>3D-Printed Shop Tools</title><link>https://www.extra-ransom.net/docs/woodworking/printed-tools/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.extra-ransom.net/docs/woodworking/printed-tools/</guid><description>
&lt;p&gt;Printable jigs and shop tools for woodworking projects — the woodworking counterpart to the &lt;a href="https://www.extra-ransom.net/docs/rod-builds/printable-rod-tools/"&gt;rodmaking tool set&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>DW745 Mobile Saw Cart (Proposed)</title><link>https://www.extra-ransom.net/docs/woodworking/dw745-mobile-saw-cart/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.extra-ransom.net/docs/woodworking/dw745-mobile-saw-cart/</guid><description>
&lt;p&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;proposed&lt;/strong&gt; build: a small plywood cart on locking casters for a DeWalt
DW745 10&amp;quot; jobsite table saw. It&amp;rsquo;s deliberately compact. The footprint is
just over the saw&amp;rsquo;s table, it comes out of &lt;strong&gt;one sheet of plywood&lt;/strong&gt;, and
it holds the saw&amp;rsquo;s accessories underneath. The saw comes off with four
knobs when it needs to go to a jobsite.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Footprint:&lt;/strong&gt; 28&amp;quot; W × 24&amp;quot; D. The DW745&amp;rsquo;s table is about 630 × 570 mm
(24.8&amp;quot; × 22.4&amp;quot;), so the cart is just over 1&amp;quot; bigger on each side.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Saw table height:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;34&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; from the floor, a standard bench height, so
a workbench can serve as outfeed. Some shops prefer ~35.5&amp;quot; (900 mm); pick
yours and plug it into the formula below.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Casters:&lt;/strong&gt; 4 of my &lt;strong&gt;step-stop locking casters&lt;/strong&gt;, one at each corner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Material:&lt;/strong&gt; ¾&amp;quot; plywood (birch or good-one-side), glue and screws.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
