&lt;h2&gt;Set the height first&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="set-the-height-first"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#set-the-height-first" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Two measurements decide the carcass height. Take them before cutting
anything:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;s&lt;/strong&gt;: from the bottom of the saw&amp;rsquo;s base (where it&amp;rsquo;ll sit on the cart)
to the top of the saw table.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;c&lt;/strong&gt;: from the caster&amp;rsquo;s mounting plate to the floor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Carcass height H = 34&amp;quot; − s − c.&lt;/strong&gt; That&amp;rsquo;s the outside height of the box,
top and bottom panels included.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Example (yours will differ)&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th style="text-align: right"&gt;s&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th style="text-align: right"&gt;c&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th style="text-align: right"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;H&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th style="text-align: right"&gt;Interior (H − 1½&amp;quot;)&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;3&amp;quot; casters&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;13.5&amp;quot;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;3.5&amp;quot;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;17&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;15.5&amp;quot;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;4&amp;quot; casters&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;13.5&amp;quot;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;4.5&amp;quot;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;16&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;14.5&amp;quot;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;5&amp;quot; casters&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;13.5&amp;quot;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;5.5&amp;quot;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;15&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;13.5&amp;quot;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The s = 13.5&amp;quot; here is only a placeholder; I don&amp;rsquo;t have a published
base-to-table height for the DW745. Measure your saw.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Cut list (one 4×8 sheet of ¾&amp;quot; plywood)&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="cut-list-one-48-sheet-of--plywood"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#cut-list-one-48-sheet-of--plywood" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Cut sizes for the example &lt;strong&gt;H = 16&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; (interior 14.5&amp;quot;). If your H is
different, change the 14.5&amp;quot; dimensions to match your interior height.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Part&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th style="text-align: right"&gt;Qty&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Size&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Top&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;28&amp;quot; × 24&amp;quot;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Saw mounts here&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Bottom&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;28&amp;quot; × 24&amp;quot;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Casters mount here&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Sides&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;2&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;14.5&amp;quot; × 24&amp;quot;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Captured between top and bottom&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Back&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;14.5&amp;quot; × 26.5&amp;quot;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Between the sides; squares and stiffens the box&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Shelf&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;26.5&amp;quot; × 22.75&amp;quot;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Set 1&amp;quot; back from the front edge, at mid-height&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That&amp;rsquo;s about 22 ft² of the sheet&amp;rsquo;s 32 ft². The offcut is enough for push
sticks and a cord cleat.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Hardware&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="hardware"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#hardware" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th style="text-align: right"&gt;Qty&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Item&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Use&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;4&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Step-stop locking casters (on hand)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;one per corner, plates flush to the corners&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;16&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;5/16&amp;quot; carriage bolts, 1½&amp;quot;, with washers and nylock nuts&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;through-bolt the caster plates; match your plate holes&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;4&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;¼&amp;quot;-20 T-nuts&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;in the top, under the saw&amp;rsquo;s base mounting holes&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;4&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;¼&amp;quot;-20 star knobs (2&amp;quot; studs) + fender washers&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;hold the saw down; removable without tools&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;~40&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1⅝&amp;quot; coarse wood screws&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;carcass&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;—&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Wood glue, edge banding (optional)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;2&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Cord cleats or hooks (offcut)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;on one side, for the cord&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Build&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="build"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#build" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Box:&lt;/strong&gt; glue and screw the sides to the bottom, then add the back
between the sides. Check that it&amp;rsquo;s square, then add the top. Fit the
shelf on cleats or dados at mid-height.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Casters:&lt;/strong&gt; bolt one under each corner of the bottom, plates as close to
the corners as they&amp;rsquo;ll go. A wider wheelbase means a less tippy cart.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Saw mount:&lt;/strong&gt; set the saw centered on the top, with the blade parallel to
the cart&amp;rsquo;s sides, and mark its base mounting holes through from above.
Drill and install the ¼&amp;quot;-20 T-nuts from underneath, then hold the saw down
with the four knobs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Finish:&lt;/strong&gt; ease the edges and give it a coat of wipe-on poly or paste
wax so sawdust doesn&amp;rsquo;t stick.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Using it safely&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="using-it-safely"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#using-it-safely" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lock all four casters before you turn the saw on.&lt;/strong&gt; Step-stop casters
that lock both the wheel and the swivel are what you want. A cart that
creeps during a rip is a kickback risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep heavy items on the bottom shelf.&lt;/strong&gt; The saw makes the cart
top-heavy, and weight down low keeps it planted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support long stock.&lt;/strong&gt; On a footprint this small, don&amp;rsquo;t rip sheet goods or
long boards without infeed and outfeed support. At 34&amp;quot; a workbench or
roller stand works.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep the rear dust port clear&lt;/strong&gt;, and run a shop-vac hose off the back
instead of through the cart.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Buy instead?&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="buy-instead"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#buy-instead" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;DeWalt makes rolling stands for this saw, the &lt;strong&gt;DE7400&lt;/strong&gt; wheeled stand and
the &lt;strong&gt;DW7451&lt;/strong&gt; compact stand. They fold, they&amp;rsquo;re quick, and they cost more
than this cart. They&amp;rsquo;re the better choice if the saw travels a lot. This
cart wins in the shop, with storage, a solid base, and casters you already
own.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Tool Links</title><link>https://www.extra-ransom.net/docs/woodworking/tool-links/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.extra-ransom.net/docs/woodworking/tool-links/</guid><description>
&lt;p&gt;Tools, suppliers, and references worth keeping track of. Add links here as they come up.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>